Implemented Vercel Web Analytics for the Angular project as requested.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` version 2.0.1 using npm
- Package added to dependencies in package.json
- Updated package-lock.json to reflect the new dependency

### 2. Configuration
Modified: `src/app/app.config.ts`
- Imported the `inject` function from `@vercel/analytics`
- Added Web Analytics initialization following the same pattern as the existing Speed Insights setup
- The `inject()` function is called within a browser check (`typeof window !== 'undefined'`) to ensure it only runs in the browser context, not during server-side rendering

### 3. Implementation Details
Following the official Vercel documentation (https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart), Angular projects should use the generic `inject` function rather than framework-specific components (which are available for React, Next.js, Vue, etc.).

The implementation:
```typescript
import { inject } from '@vercel/analytics';

// Initialize Vercel Web Analytics
if (typeof window !== 'undefined') {
  inject();
}
```

This approach:
- Matches the existing pattern used for Speed Insights in the same file
- Ensures the analytics script only loads in the browser
- Automatically tracks page views when deployed to Vercel
- Requires no additional configuration in components or templates

### 4. Verification
- ✅ Build completed successfully (npm run build)
- ✅ Tests run (1 pre-existing test failure unrelated to analytics changes)
- ✅ No linting errors introduced
- ✅ Dependencies properly installed and lock file updated

## How It Works
Once deployed to Vercel, the Web Analytics will automatically:
- Track page views across the application
- Collect visitor data in a privacy-friendly manner
- Display real-time traffic insights in the Vercel dashboard
- Work seamlessly with the existing Speed Insights integration

## Next Steps for User
1. Deploy the application to Vercel
2. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard (Analytics section)
3. View analytics data in the Vercel dashboard after deployment

The integration is complete and ready for deployment.
